{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>One who acts wisely</b> — cleaves to what is above, that is, acts wisely concerning a matter of lowliness to lower himself — he shall find good: HaShem will do good to him." "<b>And trusts in HaShem</b> — he will not desire to share spoil with the proud." "<b>Happy is he</b> — that he be made happy in the abundance of his good."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "Resolved ambiguous phrase 'דבק למעלה' as 'cleaves to what is above' (i.e., the divine), reading it as framing the subsequent gloss."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:10.424113437Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}